  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Four Year 12 students, four Year 11 students and four Year 10 students are sitting around a round table. How many ways can they be seated if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$11!$",
          "worked": "There are twelve distinct students.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=(12-1)!\\\\N&=11!\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the students all sit together in their respective year groups?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p24-q11-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2!\\times4!\\times4!\\times4!=27\\,648",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p24-q11-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Arrange three year-group blocks in a circle, then arrange the four students within each block.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Treat each year group as one block. The three blocks have $2!$ circular arrangements, and each block has $4!$ internal orders.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=(3-1)!\\times4!\\times4!\\times4!\\\\N&=2!\\times(4!)^3\\\\N&=27\\,648\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "students in the same year group are equally spaced apart?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p24-q11-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2!\\times3!\\times4!\\times4!=6\\,912",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p24-q11-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fix one Year 12 student; the year groups repeat every three seats, with two possible orders for Years 11 and 10.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Fix one Year 12 student to remove rotational duplication. Equal spacing puts the other Year 12 students in every third seat, giving $3!$ orders. Between successive Year 12 positions, Years 11 and 10 must occur in the same order throughout; there are $2!$ choices for that order. Arrange the four Year 11 students and the four Year 10 students in their respective positions.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=3!\\times2!\\times4!\\times4!\\\\N&=6\\times2\\times24\\times24\\\\N&=6\\,912\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
